        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8e39c833-afaf-5b56-84cd-92e3cbecdf75",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Smylie, Vasek Pospisil, Jack Sock, Nicole Provis, Jo-Anne Faull, Julie Richardson\n- Events: Wimbledon Championships, Indian Wells Masters, Dow Classic\n- Roles: retired professional tennis players, defending champions\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Smylie, née Sayers and sometimes known as Liz Smylie, was born on 11 April 1963 and is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\n- Elizabeth Smylie won four Grand Slam titles during her career, including one in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\n- In 1992, defending champions Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie lost in the quarterfinals of the Dow Classic doubles event to Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles title at the 2014 Wimbledon Championships.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles title at the 2015 Indian Wells Masters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "96e81c9c-742f-54a2-9e9d-0cfba09090ab",
        "text": "Page: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: Elizabeth Smylie (née Sayers, born 11 April 1963), sometimes known as Liz Smylie, is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\nPage: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: During her career, she won four Grand Slam titles, one of them in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\nPage: Vasek Pospisil. Sentence: Along with partner Jack Sock, he won the 2014 Wimbledon Championships and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters men's doubles titles.\nPage: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles. Sentence: Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie were the defending champions but were defeated in the quarterfinals by Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.",
